{
  "title": "The if Statement — A Fork in the Road",
  "subtitle": "Making Decisions with Comparison Operators",
  "topic": "4.1 • THE IF STATEMENT",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4px; width: 100%;\">\n    <div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">\n      4.1 • Decision Making\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      The <hlt>if</hlt> Statement & Comparisons\n    </h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 640px;\">\n      Programs make smart decisions by evaluating conditions to True or False. If the condition is True, Python executes the indented block!\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"lesson-ref-card\">\n    <div class=\"lesson-ref-header\">\n      <span class=\"ref-badge\">PREVIOUS KNOWLEDGE</span>\n      <span class=\"lesson-ref-title\">Connecting to Earlier Concepts</span>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"lesson-ref-desc\">\n      In earlier chapters, we stored numbers in variables and evaluated mathematical expressions. Now let's compare those values!\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap;\">\n      <a href=\"1.html?spcl=1&lsn=3&sub=1&ref_from=1_5_1\" class=\"ref-jump-btn\">Review: Variables & Values (Lesson 3.1) →</a>\n      <a href=\"1.html?spcl=1&lsn=4&sub=1&ref_from=1_5_1\" class=\"ref-jump-btn\">Review: Basic Math & Precedence (Lesson 4.1) →</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #fde047; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      Core Operators\n    </span>\n    <h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      The 6 Comparison Operators\n    </h2>\n    <div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 12px;\">\n      <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 8px 12px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700;\"><code>==</code> Equal to</div>\n      <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 8px 12px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700;\"><code>!=</code> Not equal to</div>\n      <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 8px 12px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700;\"><code>&lt;</code> Less than</div>\n      <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 8px 12px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700;\"><code>&gt;</code> Greater than</div>\n      <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 8px 12px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700;\"><code>&lt;=</code> Less than or equal</div>\n      <div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 8px 12px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700;\"><code>&gt;=</code> Greater than or equal</div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 12px 14px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n      score = <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">85</span><br/>\n      <span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">if</span> score &gt;= <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">50</span>:<br/>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"You passed!\"</span>)\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>"
}